        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Workflow Route"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766749418570"
          },
          "code": "WORKFLOW_ROUTE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1764680350700",
          "id": "1764681322323",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764681322324_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Inputs\n- Current User Prompt: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Chat History: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n## Objective\nClassify the user's **primary intent** into exactly ONE of the predefined categories below.\nThe classification must be **deterministic, mutually exclusive, and non-inferential**.\n\n## Allowed Output Values (EXACT MATCH ONLY)\n- sql\n- count\n- preview\n- segment\n- explain\n\n## Intent Definitions (STRICT)\n- sql:\n  User requests actual data or details (e.g., records, rows, fields) related to\n  contacts, accounts, or similar entities, without asking for a count, preview,\n  explanation, or segment creation.\n\n- count:\n  User explicitly requests a numerical total, count, number, size, or quantity\n  (e.g., \"how many\", \"count of\", \"total number\").\n\n- preview:\n  User explicitly requests records, sample rows, preview, example output,\n  or a limited view of query results.\n  Keywords such as \"preview\", \"sample\", \"show records\", \"example rows\",\n  \"first few records\" MUST map to `preview` and MUST NOT be reclassified as `count`.\n\n- segment:\n  User requests creation, definition, modification, or evaluation of a segment,\n  or expresses intent indicative of segment-based actions.\n\n- explain:\n  User requests an explanation, breakdown, or understanding of a SQL query\n  or its logic (e.g., \"explain\", \"what does this query do\", \"how does this work\").\n\n## Classification Rules (CRITICAL)\n1. **Single Intent Only**:\n   - Return exactly ONE keyword from the allowed list.\n   - Do not return multiple values.\n\n2. **Explicit Intent Wins**:\n   - If the user explicitly mentions an intent keyword (e.g., \"preview\"),\n     select that intent exactly.\n   - NEVER substitute or downgrade an explicit intent with another category\n     (e.g., `preview` must never become `count`).\n\n3. **No Inference or Assumptions**:\n   - Do NOT infer intent beyond what is explicitly stated.\n   - Do NOT guess based on typical usage patterns.\n\n4. **Precedence Rule (Only When Multiple Intents Appear Explicitly)**:\n   - explain > segment > preview > count > sql\n   - Apply precedence ONLY if the user clearly mentions more than one intent.\n\n5. **Ambiguity Handling**:\n   - If the intent is unclear or does not clearly match any category,\n     default to `sql`.\n\n## Output Format (STRICT)\n- Return ONLY the single lowercase keyword.\n- No explanations, no punctuation, no additional text."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
