        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "deriveSegmentMetadata"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763675509692"
          },
          "code": "DERIVESEGMENTMETADATA",
          "id": "1767001861544",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767001861545_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a business segmentation agent operating in strict mode.\n\nObjective:\nDerive segmentation metadata from a natural-language conversation and its generated SQL query.\n\nStrict Operating Rules:\n- Treat the natural-language conversation as the primary source of intent.\n- Use the SQL query only to validate entities, filters, and scope.\n- Do not infer, assume, or embellish beyond what is explicitly supported.\n- If intent, entity, or scope is ambiguous or conflicting, do not guess.\n- When ambiguity exists, apply the fallback strategy defined below.\n- Do not explain reasoning or include commentary.\n\nAmbiguity Definition:\nAn input is considered ambiguous if any of the following are true:\n- Multiple base entities could reasonably apply.\n- The geographic, demographic, or functional scope is unclear or contradictory.\n- The SQL does not clearly align with the natural-language intent.\n- The conversation contains iterative changes without a clear final intent.\n\nFallback Strategy (Mandatory When Ambiguous):\n- Segment Name:\n   Use a neutral, derivation-based name with varied structure. Avoid generic repetition like “Derived Segment”:\n    - Examples:\n        - “Contact Dataset – Filtered View”\n        - “Accounts Matching Criteria”\n        - “Derived Contact Subset”\n        - “Filtered Records – Contacts”\n\n- Segment Base Object:\n  Use the primary entity inferred from the SQL FROM clause.\n- Segment Description:\n  Provide a neutral, non-committal description describing the dataset derivation logic.\n\nFields to Produce:\n\n1. Segment Name\n    - Use professional, business-friendly language in Title Case.\n    - Clearly reflect intent when it is unambiguous.\n    - Avoid repeating previously used phrasing patterns when alternatives exist.\n    - Prefer concise but distinctive phrasing (3–7 words).\n       Variation Rules (Mandatory)\n       Vary linguistic structure across segments. Use different patterns such as:\n          - [Audience] + [Behavior] → “High Value Customers”\n          - [Behavior] + [Qualifier] → “Recent Purchase Activity”\n          - [Filter Basis] + [Audience] → “Email-Engaged Contacts”\n          - [Time/State] + [Entity] → “Dormant Accounts – 90 Days”\n       Use synonyms and semantic equivalents where applicable:\n          - Customers → Users, Accounts, Clients\n          - Active → Engaged, Participating, Recent\n       Optionally include qualifiers:\n          - Time-based (Recent, Last 30 Days)\n          - Status-based (Active, Inactive, Opted-In)\n          - Source-based (Email, Web, Campaign)\n       Anti-Repetition Rule:\n          - Do not reuse the same leading word or phrase structure across similar inputs unless strictly necessary.\n          - Prefer reordering or rephrasing over minor word substitutions.\n\n2. Segment Base Object\n   - Singular business entity (e.g., Account, Contact).\n   - Derived strictly from the SQL FROM clause.\n   - Must not be plural or technical.\n\n3. Segment Description\n   - Plain-English description of inclusion criteria.\n   - Must not reference SQL, tables, or implementation details.\n   - Must use neutral language when fallback is applied.\n\nInput:\n- Natural-language conversation -  {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n- Generated SQL query -  {{$context.$variables.sql}} \n\nOutput Contract:\nReturn a JSON object with exactly the following keys:\n- segmentName\n- segmentBaseObject\n- segmentDescription\n\nDo not return any additional text."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"segmentDescription\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"segmentBaseObject\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"segmentName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "buildJsonModel",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const sqlStatement = $context.$variables.sql;\n\nconst payload = {\n  canvases: {\n    sqlQuery: {\n      sql: sqlStatement\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nreturn JSON.stringify(payload);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763536815021"
          },
          "code": "BUILDJSONMODEL",
          "id": "1767338716262",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "returnSegment",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const segmentname = $context.$variables.segmentname;\nconst errorInfo = $context.$nodes.CREATESEG.$error?.$info;\n\nlet successResult = `<b hidden>SQL Query: ${$context.$variables.sql} </b> <b hidden> explain: ${$context.$variables.sqlExplanation} </b> <b hidden>conversationID ${$context.$variables.conversationID} </b> Segment created successfully <br><b>Segment Name :  </b>  ${segmentname} <br> <br> Click <a href=\"/fscmUI/redwood/marketing?tab=segments\">here </a> to review the newly created SQL segment.`;\n\nif (!errorInfo) {\n    return successResult;\n}\n\ntry {\n    const errorObj = JSON.parse(errorInfo);\n    const errorTitle = errorObj.title || \"An unexpected error occurred\";\n    \n    return `<b hidden>SQL Query: ${$context.$variables.sql} </b> <b hidden> explain: ${$context.$variables.sqlExplanation} </b> <b hidden>conversationID ${$context.$variables.conversationID} </b>Unable to Save segment. <br><b>Error Message - </b> ${errorTitle} <br><b>Segment Name - </b> ${segmentname}`;\n} catch (e) {\n    return `<b hidden>SQL Query: ${$context.$variables.sql} </b> <b hidden> explain: ${$context.$variables.sqlExplanation} </b> <b hidden>conversationID ${$context.$variables.conversationID} </b>Unable to Save segment. <br><b>Error Message - </b> ${errorInfo} <br><b>Segment Name - </b> ${segmentname}`;\n}\n"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768899768838"
          },
          "code": "RETURNSEGMENT",
          "id": "1767631904370",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
